{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310547,"nonce":"RfbrTlhy3zPzorzrB/xZiHUNCf4=","title":"Loading the BLADE stdlib manifest binds every packaged type's SHORT name into the root scope, so a user class with the same short name is ...","message":"OPEN, and it is the reason the embedded stdlib manifest cannot be used. Found\n2026-08-14 by three independent agents that converged on the same cause.\n\n`register_class_from_blade` / `register_enum_from_blade` /\n`register_abstract_from_blade` / `register_type_alias_from_blade`\n(compiler/src/compilation.rs ~2112/2339/2453/2543) all call\n`create_*_in_scope(short_name, ScopeId::first())` — they publish EVERY type in\nall 226 stdlib modules into the ROOT scope under its BARE SHORT NAME, packaged\ntypes included. The source-parse path never does this: it pre-registers only\nthe 12 default imports.\n\n`ast_lowering.rs::pre_register_declaration` then hits its \"already exists in\nroot scope → skip\" guard and SILENTLY DROPS the user's own declaration.\n\n**This is [[feedback_fqn_first_resolution]] exactly — bare-name lookup IS the\ndefect** — with the twist that the collision is silent on both sides.\n\nDECISIVE ISOLATION (cheapest repro, no rebuild):\n- `RZ_X_SKIPMOD=haxe.zip.Entry` ⇒ test_closure_field_call passes.\n  `compiler/haxe-std/haxe/zip/Entry.hx:33` is `typedef Entry = {…}`.\n- Skipping ONLY aliases (`NOALIASES`) ⇒ green; skipping classes/enums/\n  abstracts/methods/fields ⇒ still bad.\n- Renaming the user's CLASS `Entry`→`ZqEntryX` fixes it; renaming only the\n  FIELD does not.\n\nFAILURE CHAIN, for recognising the shape elsewhere: user `class Entry` adopts\n`haxe.zip.Entry` (an anonymous-struct typedef) → `e.body` types as `Dynamic`\ninstead of `Void-\u003eInt` → `lower_indirect_call` gets `callee.ty=Dynamic` →\nlowers to `Ptr(Void)` → and because that function builds `arg_regs` with\n`filter_map` (`ir/mir/expr/call/indirect.rs:43`) **the failed argument is\nsilently dropped**, so `check(cond, msg)` is emitted as `check(msg, 0i64)` and\n`!cond` applies Not to a string pointer → LLVM JIT panic at\n`llvm_jit_backend.rs:6680`. The `filter_map` is its own latent bug: a lowering\nfailure should not quietly shorten an argument list.\n\nBLAST RADIUS: 12 suite tests declare a short name a packaged stdlib module also\ndeclares — Entry, Option, TreeNode, BalancedTree, Box, Range, Module,\nConnection, Resource.\n\nTHE FIX (diagnosed, not landed): publish a manifest type in the root scope\nunder its QUALIFIED name when it lives in a package; reserve bare root-scope\nslots for genuinely ambient top-level types (Math, Array, String, Std, Sys,\nType…). `sym.name` keeps the short name so display and by-name comparison are\nunchanged. Same rule for a packaged enum's constructors (`Some`/`None` from\nhaxe.ds.Option take bare slots today). Best attempt so far moved the suite\n167/12/5 → **173/6/5**; not green, so the remaining 6+5 need the same\ntreatment carried further.\n\nSECONDARY, real and separately worth fixing: `is_extern_only_stdlib_base`\nskips loading sources for `Math|Array|String|Std|Class|Enum|EnumValue|Any` on\nthe premise that they have no function bodies. FALSE — `Array.hx` has\n`@:runtime inline` `iterator`/`keyValueIterator`/`map`/`filter`.\n\nTRAP THAT WASTES HOURS: the BLADE cache lives in\n`.rayzor/blade/cache/native-\u003chash\u003e/`, so `rm -f .rayzor/blade/cache/*.blade`\ncleans NOTHING and the next run silently replays cached MIR. Use `rm -rf\n.rayzor`. See [[feedback_blade_cache_clear_all_rayzor_dirs]].\n\nMain is GREEN at 184/184 (2484f6fb) by taking the source path; the manifest\npath costs ~35ms of compile (18ms vs 53ms) and is the thing to reclaim.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): FIXED d09c1f29: manifest bound SHORT names into root scope, DROPPING a same-named user class.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_bsym_manifest_binds_bare_names_shadowing_user_types` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}